# Normalise line endings so the repository does not fight its contributors.
#
# Without this file, 214 of the 217 tracked files were stored with CRLF line
# endings in the working tree. Any editor or tool that writes LF then produces a
# diff of the entire file, which buries the real change and makes review
# impossible. It also broke scripted edits that match on exact text.
#
# `* text=auto` lets Git decide per file, and `eol=lf` stores LF in the
# repository while checking out the platform convention where a file type needs
# one. Run `git add --renormalize .` once after adopting this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: no line-ending conversion, no textual diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# Canonical evidence and schema fixtures are content-addressed: a byte-level
# difference must show up as a change, not be silently normalised away.
examples/sandbox/** -text
schemas/*.json text eol=lf

# Generated reports are never reviewed by hand.
artifacts/** -text
